On Mon, Dec 7, 2009 at 9:05 PM, Dave Airlie <airlied@redhat.com> wrote:
> On Mon, 2009-12-07 at 21:01 -0800, Steven Noonan wrote:
>> Hi,
>>
>> I finally got around to compiling 2.6.32 for my primary machine, and
>> with radeon.modeset=3D1, the machine has a horrifying 33 second boot
>> delay (it stays at a black screen for the duration).
>>
>> I figured a 'git bisect v2.6.32 v2.6.31 -- drivers/gpu/drm' would
>> catch it. Hopefully this bisection helps pin down the underlying
>> problem:
>> =A0# bad: =A0[22763c5c] Linux 2.6.32
>> =A0# good: [74fca6a4] Linux 2.6.31
>> =A0# bad: =A0[df748b02] drm/ttm: fix refcounting in ttm global code.
>> =A0# good: [a513c184] drm/radeon/kms: Don't try to process irq when we a
>> =A0# good: [aadd4e17] drm/radeon: some r420s have a CP race with the DMA
>> =A0# good: [74bf2ad5] drm/kms: make fb helper work for all drivers.
>> =A0# bad: =A0[62a8ea3f] drm/radeon/kms: Remove old init path as no hw us=
e
>> =A0# good: [f0ed1f65] drm/radeon/kms: Convert R520 to new init path and
>> =A0# skip: [d4550907] drm/radeon/kms: Convert R100 to new init path (V2)
>> =A0# good: [3bc68535] drm/radeon/kms: Convert RS690/RS740 to new init pa
>> =A0# bad: =A0[c010f800] drm/radeon/kms: Convert RS600 to new init path
>>
>> Any ideas why c010f800 would cause this?
>>
>
> Wierd, it seems an unlikely change to affect this, can you boot with
> drm.debug=3D15 on the command line and see if we can glean anymore info
> about where its hanging.

Attached the dmesg with drm.debug=3D15.

> It might be good to open a bug either on kernel.org or freedesktop.org
> (against Xorg radeon driver - since we mostly hang out there).
>

Okay. Reported. https://bugs.freedesktop.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3D25506

- Steven

